00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:06,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:10,532 --> 00:00:11,783
Wait a moment!

2
00:00:12,367 --> 00:00:14,077
-I'm a lawyer!
-Stay back.

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,454
-Which police station are you from?
-Stay back.

4
00:00:17,413 --> 00:00:18,748
Mr. Uramawashi!

5
00:00:22,669 --> 00:00:26,881
That reporter,
why did he sue Mr. Uramawashi?

6
00:00:26,965 --> 00:00:31,719
I'm arresting you on suspicion
of threatening Ryutaro Sunaga.

7
00:00:33,263 --> 00:00:35,598
We tricked them.
Maybe they did it out of spite.

8
00:00:35,682 --> 00:00:38,768
If Mr. Uramawashi is gone,
what happens to me as a part-timer?

9
00:00:38,852 --> 00:00:40,854
Study architecture for a while.

10
00:00:40,937 --> 00:00:43,231
Fine, but I'm not doing overtime!

11
00:00:43,314 --> 00:00:44,691
You always go home on time.

12
00:00:44,774 --> 00:00:46,317
That's typical of you.

13
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:50,488
What's wrong, Sabayama?

14
00:00:51,114 --> 00:00:52,240
"What's wrong?"

15
00:00:55,118 --> 00:00:57,162
This is no time to be asking that!

16
00:00:57,245 --> 00:00:59,414
Mr. Uramawashi has been arrested!

17
00:00:59,497 --> 00:01:01,541
How can you be so calm about it?

18
00:01:01,624 --> 00:01:03,668
Well… you know…

19
00:01:03,751 --> 00:01:06,754
Up until now, I've acted
on Mr. Uramawashi's instructions.

20
00:01:06,838 --> 00:01:09,966
I've walked on fire many times.
But it was always fine.

21
00:01:10,049 --> 00:01:12,343
Because his plans were perfect.

22
00:01:12,427 --> 00:01:14,012
He was always four steps ahead.

23
00:01:14,095 --> 00:01:17,182
But now the man himself has been arrested.

24
00:01:19,017 --> 00:01:21,644
-Maybe we'll get caught too.
-No, that won't…

25
00:01:21,728 --> 00:01:25,231
Besides, why do we have
to keep doing these things?

26
00:01:25,857 --> 00:01:29,068
I am an architect!
A first-class architect!

27
00:01:29,152 --> 00:01:31,571
And this is
an architectural office, right?

28
00:01:31,654 --> 00:01:32,780
Calm down.

29
00:01:32,864 --> 00:01:34,908
-Let's settle down.
-Shut up!

30
00:01:36,534 --> 00:01:38,870
I'm going home.

31
00:01:44,334 --> 00:01:46,002
Sabayama!

32
00:02:07,899 --> 00:02:08,733
I never thought…

33
00:02:09,484 --> 00:02:12,445
I would end up sitting on this side.

34
00:02:14,322 --> 00:02:18,284
I don't think making Mr. Sunaga write
a retraction article about Ms. Shiramoto

35
00:02:18,368 --> 00:02:20,328
constitutes a threat.

36
00:02:20,411 --> 00:02:23,915
Besides, that article wasn't even
in the published magazine.

37
00:02:25,541 --> 00:02:26,960
Mr. Uramawashi,

38
00:02:27,043 --> 00:02:29,629
did you threaten Mr. Sunaga
with something else?

39
00:02:29,712 --> 00:02:30,797
I didn't.

40
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:33,508
Then… Why were you arrested?

41
00:02:33,591 --> 00:02:35,260
It's a warning.

42
00:02:35,843 --> 00:02:37,428
A warning?

43
00:02:39,847 --> 00:02:40,932
Huh?

44
00:02:41,724 --> 00:02:45,144
Because you're digging into
Ms. Shiramoto's wrongful conviction?

45
00:02:45,228 --> 00:02:48,398
Does it have something to do
with Representative Furuse too?

46
00:02:51,943 --> 00:02:55,488
It's a warrantless arrest.
I'll get you out as soon as possible.

47
00:02:55,571 --> 00:02:58,783
Are you planning on being
my defense lawyer?

48
00:02:59,575 --> 00:03:00,576
What?

49
00:03:04,330 --> 00:03:06,958
Don't do anything unnecessary.

50
00:03:09,627 --> 00:03:11,087
Mr. Uramawashi?

51
00:03:12,505 --> 00:03:15,925
Eto, sorry for calling you
when you're so busy.

52
00:03:16,009 --> 00:03:17,468
It's fine.

53
00:03:17,552 --> 00:03:19,512
I had things I wanted to talk about too.

54
00:03:19,595 --> 00:03:22,807
Oh, but how are things
at Mr. Kureta's office?

55
00:03:23,391 --> 00:03:26,644
Things are so bad.
We barely do any architecture.

56
00:03:26,728 --> 00:03:27,687
What?

57
00:03:28,229 --> 00:03:31,357
You barely do architecture?
At an architectural office?

58
00:03:31,441 --> 00:03:32,984
Oh, no, I mean…

59
00:03:34,027 --> 00:03:37,697
I followed Mr. Kureta
because he talked me into it,

60
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,783
but I'm sick of all the things
he makes me do.

61
00:03:41,284 --> 00:03:43,286
I shouldn't have quit Kyosue Construction.

62
00:03:45,413 --> 00:03:46,456
How about you?

63
00:03:46,539 --> 00:03:48,624
I bet you must be doing well.

64
00:03:48,708 --> 00:03:52,920
You were the star of our class, after all.
Fast-tracking to the top, huh?

65
00:03:53,004 --> 00:03:54,339
Not really.

66
00:03:56,007 --> 00:03:58,051
Did something happen?

67
00:04:00,636 --> 00:04:02,388
I've been asked to design

68
00:04:02,472 --> 00:04:06,017
a new French restaurant,
but things just won't move forward.

69
00:04:06,893 --> 00:04:09,062
They didn't like the design.

70
00:04:09,145 --> 00:04:11,981
They didn't like your design?

71
00:04:12,065 --> 00:04:13,649
Who the heck is the client?

72
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:16,944
The owner is the chef Kohei Kajiwara.

73
00:04:17,028 --> 00:04:19,614
Do you know Trompe-l'œil?
That famous three-star restaurant.

74
00:04:19,697 --> 00:04:21,783
Of course I know it!

75
00:04:21,866 --> 00:04:26,788
Well, that Chef Kajiwara
just won't give me the go-ahead.

76
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:30,625
And it seems the project
even has ties to politicians,

77
00:04:30,708 --> 00:04:35,755
so the company is pressuring me,
saying we'll be in trouble if we fail.

78
00:04:40,885 --> 00:04:45,890
I still have other clients too,
so I'm at my limit and at my wits' end.

79
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:48,893
But…

80
00:04:49,685 --> 00:04:52,355
If this project doesn't come together…

81
00:04:54,941 --> 00:04:56,192
Hey, Sabayama.

82
00:04:57,235 --> 00:04:59,654
Won't you help me with the designs
for Trompe-l'œil?

83
00:05:00,321 --> 00:05:01,322
-Me?
-Yeah.

84
00:05:01,406 --> 00:05:04,033
Your free-spirited designs
might be the breakthrough.

85
00:05:04,117 --> 00:05:07,537
-You're pulling my leg!
-I'm not!

86
00:05:09,622 --> 00:05:10,832
Please.

87
00:05:10,915 --> 00:05:12,542
Let's work together again.

88
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:24,637
Attorney Miyuki Shiramoto,

89
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,849
arrested on suspicion of murder,

90
00:05:27,932 --> 00:05:31,269
still continues to vehemently
deny the charges.

91
00:05:31,978 --> 00:05:33,521
Yukari.

92
00:05:33,604 --> 00:05:36,482
You know there's no way
I can kill someone, right?

93
00:05:37,817 --> 00:05:39,235
That's right.

94
00:05:42,947 --> 00:05:46,742
Defendant Miyuki Shiramoto
is sentenced to 15 years in prison.

95
00:05:47,326 --> 00:05:51,706
220 days of pre-trial detention
shall be included in the sentence.

96
00:05:52,331 --> 00:05:54,792
Why aren't you appealing?

97
00:05:54,876 --> 00:05:57,587
You were denying the charges
consistently before!

98
00:05:57,670 --> 00:05:59,297
Something happened, right?

99
00:06:00,506 --> 00:06:01,424
Miss,

100
00:06:02,175 --> 00:06:03,676
please talk to me.

101
00:06:05,303 --> 00:06:09,765
Ms. Shiramoto, if you don't hurry,
the appeal deadline will pass.

102
00:06:11,309 --> 00:06:12,518
Miss…

103
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:19,650
Miss, please tell me what happened.

104
00:06:20,318 --> 00:06:21,861
This isn't right!

105
00:06:22,862 --> 00:06:24,071
I'm sorry,

106
00:06:25,239 --> 00:06:26,657
Yukari.

107
00:06:30,286 --> 00:06:33,623
And then, I barely made it to the trial.

108
00:06:33,706 --> 00:06:35,458
It was a really close call.

109
00:06:35,541 --> 00:06:38,544
I wish someone had woken me up.

110
00:06:38,628 --> 00:06:40,546
You're not asking about it today?

111
00:06:41,464 --> 00:06:42,715
The case, I mean.

112
00:06:43,466 --> 00:06:48,095
If I come here
and just ask about the case every time,

113
00:06:48,596 --> 00:06:51,515
it would just make you sad, Ms. Shiramoto.

114
00:06:54,518 --> 00:06:55,728
Thank you.

115
00:06:59,315 --> 00:07:03,653
You know that lawyer we always talk about?

116
00:07:04,487 --> 00:07:05,446
Yes.

117
00:07:06,322 --> 00:07:08,074
That strange man?

118
00:07:09,242 --> 00:07:11,744
He was suddenly arrested.

119
00:07:11,827 --> 00:07:12,912
What?

120
00:07:13,788 --> 00:07:15,331
That lawyer…

121
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:21,546
His name is Naoto Uramawashi.

122
00:07:22,922 --> 00:07:24,465
Do you know him?

123
00:07:27,969 --> 00:07:29,178
No.

124
00:07:31,514 --> 00:07:32,932
Is that so?

125
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:38,729
-Chef Kajiwara is here.
-Oh, let him in.

126
00:07:45,778 --> 00:07:48,030
Chef Kajiwara, I was waiting for you.

127
00:07:50,032 --> 00:07:51,200
Come in.

128
00:07:53,536 --> 00:07:56,497
We'd like you to manage the restaurant,
the food court,

129
00:07:56,581 --> 00:07:59,333
and every section related to food.

130
00:07:59,417 --> 00:08:01,544
You will be the general manager.

131
00:08:02,253 --> 00:08:05,381
Of course, we're counting on you
for future plans as well.

132
00:08:06,424 --> 00:08:07,842
Thank you very much.

133
00:08:08,509 --> 00:08:12,680
I'm showcasing a new menu
today, so I must go.

134
00:08:12,763 --> 00:08:15,850
Okay, please keep up the good work.

135
00:08:17,810 --> 00:08:19,979
How are things with the new restaurant?

136
00:08:20,062 --> 00:08:24,317
I haven't been presented
with a satisfying design yet.

137
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,986
Kyosue Construction, right?

138
00:08:27,570 --> 00:08:30,281
I introduced them because I heard
they were capable.

139
00:08:30,364 --> 00:08:32,158
I see…

140
00:08:32,241 --> 00:08:34,452
I'll contact them on my end.

141
00:08:36,746 --> 00:08:40,333
The new restaurant won't just
get your name out into the world.

142
00:08:40,416 --> 00:08:43,586
It will be a crucial cornerstone
for our plans.

143
00:08:44,211 --> 00:08:47,715
Let's both put more effort into it.

144
00:08:47,798 --> 00:08:49,675
Yes. Please, excuse me.

145
00:08:56,766 --> 00:08:58,601
MOST EXCEPTIONAL RESTAURANT OF THE YEAR

146
00:09:01,854 --> 00:09:04,607
For appetizers,
the cross-section should face 6 o'clock.

147
00:09:04,690 --> 00:09:05,524
Okay.

148
00:09:05,608 --> 00:09:08,152
The main dishes
should be in front to create depth.

149
00:09:08,235 --> 00:09:09,070
Yes.

150
00:09:10,738 --> 00:09:13,282
This plate is missing sauce.
Add a little more.

151
00:09:13,366 --> 00:09:14,575
Understood.

152
00:09:16,077 --> 00:09:17,912
Be careful not to ruin the sugar work.

153
00:09:17,995 --> 00:09:19,622
Yes, understood.

154
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:25,419
-Bonjour, chef.
-How are the preparations?

155
00:09:25,503 --> 00:09:27,505
Everything will be ready shortly.

156
00:09:27,588 --> 00:09:28,589
I see.

157
00:09:33,094 --> 00:09:34,345
Do you want a taste?

158
00:09:35,304 --> 00:09:36,764
No, it's fine.

159
00:09:37,973 --> 00:09:38,933
Understood.

160
00:09:39,016 --> 00:09:42,269
I leave everything up to you.
Should be no problem, right?

161
00:09:43,229 --> 00:09:44,355
Yes.

162
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:48,234
The cauliflower soup
has such a pleasant hint of hazelnut!

163
00:09:48,317 --> 00:09:49,485
It's wonderful!

164
00:09:49,568 --> 00:09:50,486
Thank you.

165
00:09:50,569 --> 00:09:53,781
The apple sauce on the meat dish
tasted like fall!

166
00:09:53,864 --> 00:09:56,325
-And the colorful salmon…
-Higuchi.

167
00:09:56,409 --> 00:09:59,412
You're lucky to have
such a wonderful master.

168
00:09:59,495 --> 00:10:02,373
You need to become like Chef Kajiwara.

169
00:10:06,877 --> 00:10:08,212
I agree.

170
00:10:09,046 --> 00:10:10,673
Can you face this way?

171
00:10:11,757 --> 00:10:13,134
Thank you!

172
00:10:13,217 --> 00:10:14,510
This way, please.

173
00:10:14,593 --> 00:10:15,511
WEEKLY TIMES

174
00:10:15,594 --> 00:10:17,596
There you are! I heard the news.

175
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:20,683
Mr. Uramawashi got arrested

176
00:10:22,017 --> 00:10:25,187
And Sunaga is the one
who sued him for damages?

177
00:10:25,813 --> 00:10:27,398
That's right.

178
00:10:27,481 --> 00:10:30,401
We thought we had him cornered, but…

179
00:10:30,484 --> 00:10:33,529
You'll have to just ask him directly.

180
00:10:37,241 --> 00:10:41,078
Mr. Kureta,
I've decided to help Eto with his work.

181
00:10:41,162 --> 00:10:43,622
Eto from your days at Kyosue Construction?

182
00:10:43,706 --> 00:10:44,540
Yes.

183
00:10:44,623 --> 00:10:47,960
Of course,
I'll still do my job here properly.

184
00:10:48,043 --> 00:10:49,170
Sure.

185
00:10:52,798 --> 00:10:54,842
What do you mean you were threatened?

186
00:10:54,925 --> 00:10:57,428
Wasn't that basically a threat?

187
00:10:59,263 --> 00:11:02,516
Besides, I was told to sue him
for damages.

188
00:11:03,184 --> 00:11:04,018
By whom?

189
00:11:04,602 --> 00:11:05,603
Well…

190
00:11:06,187 --> 00:11:09,064
If you don't tell me,
I'll expose your fabricated articles.

191
00:11:10,065 --> 00:11:12,693
-You're threatening me too?
-Threatening you?

192
00:11:12,776 --> 00:11:15,279
You did write fake articles, right?

193
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:22,077
Fine.

194
00:11:24,163 --> 00:11:28,876
I was told that if I sued,
I wouldn't have to face threats like that.

195
00:11:28,959 --> 00:11:30,211
But by whom?

196
00:11:31,086 --> 00:11:33,255
A Korean man visited me.

197
00:11:33,923 --> 00:11:37,426
He told me,
"We'll handle the rest, don't worry."

198
00:11:41,514 --> 00:11:44,808
I won't take orders from you anymore.

199
00:11:44,892 --> 00:11:46,101
Why is that?

200
00:11:46,685 --> 00:11:48,604
Don't ask me "why"!

201
00:11:48,687 --> 00:11:51,398
Because I am an architect!

202
00:11:51,482 --> 00:11:52,733
Are you listening?

203
00:11:52,816 --> 00:11:55,152
Yeah, and?

204
00:11:55,903 --> 00:11:57,571
Why does an architect like me

205
00:11:57,655 --> 00:12:00,032
always have to cross
such dangerous bridges…

206
00:12:04,662 --> 00:12:07,998
I mean, design such dangerous bridges?

207
00:12:10,334 --> 00:12:12,711
Remember Eto from Kyosue Construction?

208
00:12:12,795 --> 00:12:14,046
I remember.

209
00:12:14,547 --> 00:12:19,843
I'm going to help create a design
for a new Trompe-l'œil restaurant.

210
00:12:21,053 --> 00:12:23,430
I've been to that place a few times.

211
00:12:24,265 --> 00:12:26,600
If this project comes together nicely…

212
00:12:28,227 --> 00:12:30,020
No, nothing.

213
00:12:31,063 --> 00:12:34,817
Also, may I use your office?

214
00:12:35,526 --> 00:12:38,654
It's an important project,
so I want to concentrate.

215
00:12:38,737 --> 00:12:40,447
Feel free.

216
00:12:42,616 --> 00:12:43,784
Well then.

217
00:12:49,832 --> 00:12:53,836
We may never meet again.

218
00:12:57,715 --> 00:12:58,799
Thanks for everything.

219
00:13:08,350 --> 00:13:11,020
This is a flawless design.

220
00:13:11,770 --> 00:13:16,191
Knowing you, I bet you faithfully
materialized Chef Kajiwara's order.

221
00:13:17,484 --> 00:13:18,444
Yeah.

222
00:13:19,153 --> 00:13:21,155
What did he request?

223
00:13:23,032 --> 00:13:24,575
Well…

224
00:13:26,368 --> 00:13:29,913
Chef Kajiwara only gives
the final judgment.

225
00:13:29,997 --> 00:13:31,248
What?

226
00:13:31,332 --> 00:13:32,833
Then who made the order?

227
00:13:32,916 --> 00:13:35,628
Higuchi. The sous chef.

228
00:13:36,337 --> 00:13:38,005
I'm counting on you.

229
00:13:38,088 --> 00:13:39,214
Yes.

230
00:13:43,844 --> 00:13:45,346
Where is Chef Kajiwara going?

231
00:13:45,429 --> 00:13:49,475
I've been with Chef Kajiwara
for 20 years now.

232
00:13:49,558 --> 00:13:54,438
He taught me everything
about cooking and this restaurant.

233
00:13:55,939 --> 00:13:58,192
I understand well what he wants.

234
00:13:58,692 --> 00:14:01,779
Please leave the new restaurant to me.

235
00:14:01,862 --> 00:14:06,033
So this design was made with Mr. Higuchi?

236
00:14:06,116 --> 00:14:10,287
Yes, he said
this was what Chef Kajiwara wanted.

237
00:14:11,121 --> 00:14:15,042
Yet, Chef Kajiwara
won't give final approval.

238
00:14:15,584 --> 00:14:16,877
Why?

239
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:19,713
I don't know! That's why I'm stuck.

240
00:14:23,634 --> 00:14:27,513
If the design isn't put together
by the deadline…

241
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:30,182
A simple "sorry" won't cut it.

242
00:14:32,476 --> 00:14:33,602
All right,

243
00:14:34,144 --> 00:14:38,023
for now, can I talk to Mr. Higuchi too?

244
00:14:39,608 --> 00:14:42,778
Set up the kitchen like a stage,

245
00:14:43,404 --> 00:14:46,031
and light only the kitchen brightly.

246
00:14:46,115 --> 00:14:51,161
Dim the seating area a bit,
so the kitchen stands out.

247
00:14:51,787 --> 00:14:53,163
He wants customers to see

248
00:14:53,247 --> 00:14:56,542
everything right in front of them,
from cooking to plating.

249
00:14:57,876 --> 00:15:00,129
A restaurant where the chef is the star?

250
00:15:00,212 --> 00:15:03,465
Yes, because our chef
is Mr. Kohei Kajiwara.

251
00:15:03,549 --> 00:15:04,758
I see.

252
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:08,595
Yet you still can't get approval
from the man himself?

253
00:15:08,679 --> 00:15:09,513
Yes…

254
00:15:10,097 --> 00:15:13,892
I thought he would be pleased
with this design.

255
00:15:27,698 --> 00:15:28,907
How's it going?

256
00:15:28,991 --> 00:15:31,326
Don't just walk in uninvited!

257
00:15:34,788 --> 00:15:37,041
And don't look at my stuff!

258
00:15:39,084 --> 00:15:40,335
I think…

259
00:15:40,878 --> 00:15:43,839
It's more boring than your usual designs.

260
00:15:43,922 --> 00:15:44,840
Huh?

261
00:15:44,923 --> 00:15:46,592
That's Trompe-l'œil, right?

262
00:15:47,259 --> 00:15:48,093
Yeah.

263
00:15:48,177 --> 00:15:54,058
That Chef Kajiwara is eccentric,
or rather, quite a weirdo, isn't he?

264
00:15:55,726 --> 00:15:59,605
I bet it will be tough, but do your best.

265
00:16:08,489 --> 00:16:09,740
Chef Kajiwara?

266
00:16:10,699 --> 00:16:11,950
A weirdo?

267
00:16:21,502 --> 00:16:23,545
KOHEI KAJIWARA

268
00:16:28,884 --> 00:16:31,178
What a lovely office.

269
00:16:32,221 --> 00:16:33,764
Thank you for contacting me.

270
00:16:33,847 --> 00:16:35,015
It's nothing.

271
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,102
I spent every day in loneliness.

272
00:16:38,644 --> 00:16:39,478
What?

273
00:16:39,561 --> 00:16:41,772
Because I went so long without seeing you.

274
00:16:43,607 --> 00:16:45,275
I wanted to see you too.

275
00:16:45,818 --> 00:16:47,152
Because…

276
00:16:47,736 --> 00:16:50,823
I need to ask you something, Donghyuk.

277
00:16:52,407 --> 00:16:53,575
What is it?

278
00:16:56,411 --> 00:16:59,414
Do you know Mr. Sunaga from Weekly Times?

279
00:16:59,998 --> 00:17:01,375
Mr. Sunaga?

280
00:17:03,043 --> 00:17:07,005
Yes, he's an interesting person.

281
00:17:08,799 --> 00:17:11,593
Hoshino apartments'
Mr. Hoshino also told me…

282
00:17:12,344 --> 00:17:17,307
It was you who bought his land
in Konan City, right?

283
00:17:18,767 --> 00:17:22,896
Was that your goal from the start,
when you approached that property?

284
00:17:25,190 --> 00:17:26,608
Well, what is it?

285
00:17:30,070 --> 00:17:32,239
The time I spent with you

286
00:17:33,657 --> 00:17:35,576
was a lot of fun.

287
00:17:37,995 --> 00:17:41,206
Whenever I met you, I always thought this…

288
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:45,127
You are naively honest.

289
00:17:49,381 --> 00:17:50,716
Donghyuk,

290
00:17:52,009 --> 00:17:53,719
who on earth are you?

291
00:17:59,016 --> 00:18:00,893
Whoever I am,

292
00:18:01,810 --> 00:18:04,146
is none of your business.

293
00:18:17,034 --> 00:18:20,120
I thoroughly researched Chef Kajiwara
and made this.

294
00:18:20,746 --> 00:18:22,247
What is this?

295
00:18:22,915 --> 00:18:26,084
I thought it might be interesting
if a Japanese paper umbrella

296
00:18:26,168 --> 00:18:30,214
stood tall right in the middle
of a French restaurant.

297
00:18:32,925 --> 00:18:34,259
Is it no good?

298
00:18:35,052 --> 00:18:38,013
It's a bit too eccentric, I suppose.

299
00:18:42,351 --> 00:18:43,602
What is this?

300
00:18:43,685 --> 00:18:45,729
The new design, apparently.

301
00:18:45,812 --> 00:18:46,688
Chef Kajiwara,

302
00:18:47,272 --> 00:18:49,691
I was in charge of this design.

303
00:18:49,775 --> 00:18:52,069
My name is Sabayama. I'm an architect.

304
00:18:52,986 --> 00:18:56,698
This design was created
based on a paper umbrella.

305
00:18:56,782 --> 00:18:58,075
One from Gifu Prefecture.

306
00:18:58,700 --> 00:18:59,785
Gifu?

307
00:18:59,868 --> 00:19:03,497
Chef, if I recall,
you are originally from Gifu.

308
00:19:05,582 --> 00:19:08,418
This umbrella is the main pillar.

309
00:19:09,336 --> 00:19:14,007
I imagined it as you,
who is the main pillar of this restaurant.

310
00:19:19,054 --> 00:19:21,807
Escoffier ran his kitchen
like a military brigade.

311
00:19:21,890 --> 00:19:24,351
A brigade without a general will fail.

312
00:19:24,434 --> 00:19:29,189
What he truly cared about was the time
it took for a dish to reach the table.

313
00:19:30,899 --> 00:19:32,901
Brillat-Savarin said that…

314
00:19:33,527 --> 00:19:37,864
The dining table is the only place
where a person is never bored.

315
00:19:41,576 --> 00:19:42,619
What?

316
00:19:42,703 --> 00:19:47,541
Excuse me, Kajiwara
sometimes uses strange expressions.

317
00:19:50,794 --> 00:19:53,922
Escoffier, Brillat-Savarin.

318
00:19:56,049 --> 00:19:58,051
He really is a weirdo.

319
00:20:01,555 --> 00:20:04,599
He's like Mr. Uramawashi.

320
00:20:05,434 --> 00:20:07,561
You mean that Mr. Uramawashi?

321
00:20:08,145 --> 00:20:09,187
Oh, you remember?

322
00:20:09,271 --> 00:20:11,106
Of course.

323
00:20:11,189 --> 00:20:14,234
Come to think of it,
he became a lawyer, right?

324
00:20:14,318 --> 00:20:16,737
-Do you still hang out with him?
-What?

325
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:20,198
Well, you could say that, yeah.

326
00:20:28,999 --> 00:20:31,293
Did your health take a turn for the worse?

327
00:20:32,127 --> 00:20:34,588
My blood pressure is a bit high.

328
00:20:35,255 --> 00:20:36,631
You have to be careful.

329
00:20:38,925 --> 00:20:40,010
Chef,

330
00:20:40,761 --> 00:20:43,096
I've wanted to ask you for a while.

331
00:20:43,930 --> 00:20:47,476
Why won't you approve Eto's design?

332
00:20:49,102 --> 00:20:51,063
His design is wonderful.

333
00:20:52,147 --> 00:20:56,526
If I'm to be in charge of the new
restaurant, I want that design.

334
00:20:57,402 --> 00:20:59,029
About that…

335
00:21:17,714 --> 00:21:19,966
"We may never meet again."

336
00:21:21,176 --> 00:21:22,677
Didn't you say that?

337
00:21:27,391 --> 00:21:28,475
Could you…

338
00:21:29,017 --> 00:21:30,977
Take a look at this for a moment?

339
00:21:33,730 --> 00:21:35,524
A well-made design.

340
00:21:36,024 --> 00:21:38,276
However, it won't pass.

341
00:21:39,069 --> 00:21:40,362
How do you know?

342
00:21:40,946 --> 00:21:44,616
It is not what Chef Kajiwara ordered.

343
00:21:45,867 --> 00:21:46,785
Am I right?

344
00:21:48,537 --> 00:21:49,454
Yes.

345
00:21:50,247 --> 00:21:54,835
Actually, it was designed after talking
with Mr. Higuchi, the sous chef.

346
00:21:55,627 --> 00:22:00,090
Mr. Higuchi was apparently entrusted
with the design, but in the end,

347
00:22:00,173 --> 00:22:04,177
Chef Kajiwara wouldn't give
the final approval, so they're stuck.

348
00:22:04,261 --> 00:22:06,221
Did you meet Chef Kajiwara?

349
00:22:06,304 --> 00:22:09,766
I met him, but he was a really weird guy.

350
00:22:09,850 --> 00:22:11,726
I couldn't understand what he said.

351
00:22:13,186 --> 00:22:15,897
And that's why you came here today?

352
00:22:16,731 --> 00:22:18,984
-Because I'm a weirdo.
-Yes.

353
00:22:19,693 --> 00:22:21,611
No! I didn't mean it that way.

354
00:22:25,699 --> 00:22:28,785
Gaudí had an assistant named Berenguer.

355
00:22:28,869 --> 00:22:33,081
For 30 years, he turned
Gaudí's concepts into drawings,

356
00:22:33,165 --> 00:22:37,794
managed the construction sites,
and brought the architecture into reality.

357
00:22:39,129 --> 00:22:43,133
But the fame belonged to Gaudí alone.

358
00:22:43,758 --> 00:22:45,260
And?

359
00:22:46,094 --> 00:22:50,765
I wonder what Berenguer
actually felt, back then.

360
00:22:51,433 --> 00:22:52,434
What?

361
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:59,566
You should be able to draw it too.

362
00:23:00,609 --> 00:23:02,402
The blueprint of lies.

363
00:23:06,990 --> 00:23:07,782
BORROWING

364
00:23:07,866 --> 00:23:12,495
To give shape to a blueprint of lies,
you need a draft.

365
00:23:15,999 --> 00:23:17,751
I can't do it alone.

366
00:23:20,837 --> 00:23:21,963
BORROWING

367
00:23:22,047 --> 00:23:25,258
-I'll start working on the model.
-Yeah, make it at 1:50 scale.

368
00:23:25,342 --> 00:23:27,260
We're low on styrene board, I'll buy some.

369
00:23:27,344 --> 00:23:28,261
Please do.

370
00:23:28,345 --> 00:23:29,679
I have no other choice.

371
00:23:36,436 --> 00:23:37,479
Hello.

372
00:23:37,562 --> 00:23:39,189
Hello.

373
00:23:42,317 --> 00:23:44,653
Please! Help me out!

374
00:23:46,738 --> 00:23:50,367
What the… you went to visit
with Mr. Uramawashi after all.

375
00:23:50,450 --> 00:23:51,701
I had no choice!

376
00:23:51,785 --> 00:23:54,871
I couldn't understand a thing
Chef Kajiwara was saying.

377
00:23:54,955 --> 00:23:57,874
So you went to ask him
how to draw up the blueprints?

378
00:23:57,958 --> 00:23:58,792
Yes.

379
00:23:58,875 --> 00:24:02,796
But since his face is known to the target,
he wants us to cooperate.

380
00:24:02,879 --> 00:24:04,381
Isn't he asking too much?

381
00:24:04,464 --> 00:24:05,757
Come on, it's fine.

382
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:09,177
This is basically
Mr. Uramawashi asking us.

383
00:24:09,678 --> 00:24:12,764
I've wanted to ask this for a while,

384
00:24:13,431 --> 00:24:16,059
but why do you all
go so far for Mr. Uramawashi?

385
00:24:16,142 --> 00:24:18,353
It's because we owe him
a debt of gratitude.

386
00:24:18,436 --> 00:24:19,312
Gratitude?

387
00:24:19,396 --> 00:24:23,149
There's no use hiding it. Right, Habu?

388
00:24:23,233 --> 00:24:24,276
Yeah.

389
00:24:24,859 --> 00:24:26,736
Back in the day,

390
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:30,490
I hit on a girl, but it turned out
she was waiting for her boyfriend.

391
00:24:30,573 --> 00:24:32,742
He came at me,

392
00:24:32,826 --> 00:24:35,453
so I shoved him away,
and he hit his head a bit.

393
00:24:35,537 --> 00:24:38,081
The guy just happened to be Yakuza.

394
00:24:38,790 --> 00:24:40,709
And things got really complicated.

395
00:24:40,792 --> 00:24:45,463
Then, Mr. Uramawashi fabricated
some evidence to get me out of trouble.

396
00:24:46,047 --> 00:24:46,965
The heck?

397
00:24:47,048 --> 00:24:48,550
Come on, Ms. Konno, you too.

398
00:24:48,633 --> 00:24:51,469
-I have to say it too?
-We're on the subject.

399
00:24:51,553 --> 00:24:52,637
Well…

400
00:24:53,138 --> 00:24:57,767
As for me, I got into host clubs
and ended up in debt.

401
00:24:57,851 --> 00:24:58,810
Host clubs?

402
00:24:58,893 --> 00:25:01,104
Yeah, they ran a rip-off operation.

403
00:25:01,187 --> 00:25:04,149
They charged me
some ridiculous interest on my debt,

404
00:25:04,232 --> 00:25:07,902
but Mr. Uramawashi wiped it all out,
including the unpaid tab.

405
00:25:07,986 --> 00:25:12,198
I just kind of admired
Mr. Uramawashi's methods.

406
00:25:12,282 --> 00:25:13,116
That's all.

407
00:25:13,199 --> 00:25:14,701
-Wait, that's all?
-Yeah.

408
00:25:14,784 --> 00:25:18,330
Well, one way or another,
everyone owes that man a favor.

409
00:25:19,789 --> 00:25:21,916
Shall we brainstorm the plan?

410
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,710
-Okay.
-Ça va?

411
00:25:26,296 --> 00:25:27,464
Ça va?

412
00:25:30,008 --> 00:25:31,843
I'm not a French greeting!

413
00:25:31,926 --> 00:25:34,471
Shall I play a college girl this time?

414
00:25:34,554 --> 00:25:35,764
A complete miscast.

415
00:25:35,847 --> 00:25:37,057
I'll come up with ideas.

416
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:39,267
You're just going to use AI anyway!

417
00:26:15,595 --> 00:26:16,679
It's done.

418
00:26:17,347 --> 00:26:20,183
Our blueprint of lies.

419
00:26:27,399 --> 00:26:30,276
I work as a food coordinator.

420
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:32,695
My name is Chizuru Saeki.

421
00:26:33,321 --> 00:26:37,200
Actually, I received a request
from a wealthy investor.

422
00:26:37,283 --> 00:26:41,788
They would love to open a restaurant
with you as the chef, Mr. Higuchi.

423
00:26:42,414 --> 00:26:43,415
I see.

424
00:26:43,498 --> 00:26:46,751
Then, regarding the details…

425
00:26:49,587 --> 00:26:51,256
My client himself will explain.

426
00:26:51,339 --> 00:26:54,968
Chef Higuchi, nice to meet you.
My name is Sawahara.

427
00:26:59,139 --> 00:27:01,182
I'll get straight to the point.

428
00:27:01,266 --> 00:27:03,560
I offer you three times
your current salary.

429
00:27:03,643 --> 00:27:07,021
The property, interior, and staff,
I will prepare everything.

430
00:27:07,105 --> 00:27:10,775
You just need to focus purely on cooking.

431
00:27:11,609 --> 00:27:12,444
In fact,

432
00:27:13,278 --> 00:27:15,947
we are already moving forward
with the design.

433
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:18,950
Something like this.

434
00:27:20,493 --> 00:27:21,578
The kitchen

435
00:27:21,661 --> 00:27:24,581
will be visible from anywhere
inside the restaurant.

436
00:27:24,664 --> 00:27:28,376
The guests can enjoy the chef's cooking
like a performance,

437
00:27:28,460 --> 00:27:31,671
and further savor the dish itself.

438
00:27:31,754 --> 00:27:35,800
A style where you are truly
the star of the show.

439
00:27:40,930 --> 00:27:45,226
If you'd like, shall we go take a look
at the actual property right now?

440
00:27:45,894 --> 00:27:46,769
Huh?

441
00:27:47,395 --> 00:27:48,563
Right now?

442
00:27:49,272 --> 00:27:50,565
-Yes.
-Yes.

443
00:27:52,025 --> 00:27:54,777
I am Kawakami from Saliant Real Estate.

444
00:27:56,529 --> 00:27:58,072
Please, come on in.

445
00:28:11,461 --> 00:28:13,671
May I take a look at the kitchen?

446
00:28:13,755 --> 00:28:15,173
Sure, right this way.

447
00:28:21,179 --> 00:28:22,722
It has everything we need.

448
00:28:22,805 --> 00:28:25,600
This restaurant actually closed down
just the other day.

449
00:28:25,683 --> 00:28:28,853
Of course, you could use it as is,

450
00:28:28,937 --> 00:28:32,732
but we can also renovate it
like the blueprint earlier. Your call.

451
00:28:32,815 --> 00:28:34,859
Well, if I'm going to do it…

452
00:28:35,443 --> 00:28:37,529
You prefer the design we showed you.

453
00:28:37,612 --> 00:28:38,863
Yes, that's right.

454
00:29:10,103 --> 00:29:11,729
Mr. Sawahara,

455
00:29:12,814 --> 00:29:15,942
if you'd like, why don't we talk
at my restaurant?

456
00:29:16,985 --> 00:29:17,986
I'd love to.

457
00:29:19,863 --> 00:29:23,825
Frankly, what do you think
about this proposal?

458
00:29:24,701 --> 00:29:25,702
To be honest,

459
00:29:26,244 --> 00:29:29,372
when I was at that property,
I could picture it.

460
00:29:30,582 --> 00:29:33,001
Myself standing in the spotlight.

461
00:29:33,084 --> 00:29:36,421
So, you will positively consider it, then?

462
00:29:36,504 --> 00:29:37,714
Yes.

463
00:29:37,797 --> 00:29:39,591
Thank you very much.

464
00:29:40,550 --> 00:29:44,053
But, I have one request.

465
00:29:44,804 --> 00:29:45,847
What might that be?

466
00:29:47,891 --> 00:29:53,146
I want to create
a restaurant that surpasses Trompe-l'œil.

467
00:29:53,688 --> 00:29:57,066
However, simply poaching you
won't make that a reality.

468
00:29:57,150 --> 00:29:58,818
Because you are merely

469
00:29:59,569 --> 00:30:03,197
the sous chef under Chef Kajiwara.

470
00:30:07,660 --> 00:30:09,329
What are you trying to say?

471
00:30:09,954 --> 00:30:11,706
I need something that can serve

472
00:30:11,789 --> 00:30:15,251
as the main selling point
of your restaurant, Chef Higuchi.

473
00:30:17,462 --> 00:30:22,383
I had intended
to keep this to myself, but…

474
00:30:23,927 --> 00:30:28,514
For about a year now,
from course composition,

475
00:30:29,515 --> 00:30:33,770
ingredient sourcing and ordering,
menu development,

476
00:30:33,853 --> 00:30:37,857
choosing wine pairings, to even pricing…

477
00:30:38,608 --> 00:30:42,070
I have been entrusted with everything
in the restaurant.

478
00:30:44,781 --> 00:30:47,200
That's hard to believe.

479
00:30:47,283 --> 00:30:49,410
Chef Kajiwara isn't involved at all?

480
00:30:50,411 --> 00:30:52,455
From what I've heard,

481
00:30:52,538 --> 00:30:56,042
Trompe-l'œil is moving forward
with plans for a new location,

482
00:30:56,125 --> 00:31:01,255
but if what you're saying is true,
could that new location

483
00:31:01,756 --> 00:31:04,092
be a restaurant for you?

484
00:31:06,135 --> 00:31:08,346
That was supposed to be the case, but…

485
00:31:09,555 --> 00:31:11,224
About that…

486
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:16,562
I have no intention
of leaving the new restaurant to you.

487
00:31:18,106 --> 00:31:19,607
How could that be…

488
00:31:20,733 --> 00:31:27,115
Even when I frantically created menus,
composed courses, made customers happy,

489
00:31:27,657 --> 00:31:29,784
the one who took credit was always…

490
00:31:38,251 --> 00:31:39,711
For the past year,

491
00:31:39,794 --> 00:31:42,922
when I make dishes,
he doesn't taste them at all.

492
00:31:43,006 --> 00:31:44,382
In other words,

493
00:31:45,299 --> 00:31:50,680
my cooking no longer
requires his checking.

494
00:31:52,306 --> 00:31:55,226
It means my cooking
has reached a level good enough

495
00:31:56,853 --> 00:32:01,149
to be served under the name
of Kohei Kajiwara.

496
00:32:03,109 --> 00:32:05,737
I've stood shoulder to shoulder
with Kajiwara.

497
00:32:06,320 --> 00:32:08,656
Surpassing him is only a matter of time.

498
00:32:10,450 --> 00:32:11,576
Besides…

499
00:32:11,659 --> 00:32:13,453
-Besides?
-No.

500
00:32:13,536 --> 00:32:15,329
Just between you and me…

501
00:32:15,413 --> 00:32:17,957
It seems his health isn't doing so well.

502
00:32:18,583 --> 00:32:19,459
Huh?

503
00:32:20,501 --> 00:32:22,295
He's always taking medication.

504
00:32:23,796 --> 00:32:26,674
So please rest assured, Mr. Sawahara.

505
00:32:29,093 --> 00:32:32,597
I will definitely surpass this restaurant.

506
00:32:34,182 --> 00:32:36,517
Yes, that is more than enough.

507
00:32:39,896 --> 00:32:41,939
I feel incredibly reassured.

508
00:32:47,695 --> 00:32:49,447
He's quite the gentleman,

509
00:32:50,198 --> 00:32:51,866
that guy Donghyuk.

510
00:32:51,949 --> 00:32:53,326
A gentleman?

511
00:32:53,409 --> 00:32:58,581
By getting me arrested,
he clearly demonstrated where he stands.

512
00:32:59,165 --> 00:33:00,083
Huh?

513
00:33:00,708 --> 00:33:03,252
So he was an enemy, after all.

514
00:33:04,670 --> 00:33:06,297
Could it be…

515
00:33:07,673 --> 00:33:11,928
It would be best
if Sunaga's article got published.

516
00:33:12,011 --> 00:33:14,388
But if it isn't published,

517
00:33:14,472 --> 00:33:17,892
we would know that Furuse
pressured people not to publish it.

518
00:33:18,559 --> 00:33:21,479
If that happened,
someone would make a move.

519
00:33:21,979 --> 00:33:24,148
And that someone was Donghyuk.

520
00:33:25,149 --> 00:33:28,653
By doing so, it became clear
who was on the enemy side,

521
00:33:29,237 --> 00:33:31,739
and we could also see Furuse's movements.

522
00:33:31,823 --> 00:33:34,158
You purposely got arrested

523
00:33:35,118 --> 00:33:36,911
just to get Furuse to act.

524
00:33:39,038 --> 00:33:42,083
Mr. Uramawashi,
you must have a bigger endgame.

525
00:33:42,708 --> 00:33:45,253
Isn't it about time you told me?

526
00:33:46,003 --> 00:33:47,004
Sorry.

527
00:33:48,005 --> 00:33:50,216
The next guest is waiting.

528
00:33:52,635 --> 00:33:53,845
I see,

529
00:33:53,928 --> 00:33:57,140
so there really was a Berenguer
behind Gaudí.

530
00:33:58,015 --> 00:34:01,227
How did you realize that, Mr. Uramawashi?

531
00:34:01,310 --> 00:34:03,437
I went to Trompe-l'œil a few times.

532
00:34:04,147 --> 00:34:07,024
At some point, the taste changed slightly.

533
00:34:09,110 --> 00:34:10,486
A certain quirk.

534
00:34:11,070 --> 00:34:11,988
A quirk?

535
00:34:12,071 --> 00:34:14,532
Berenguer imposed
his own tastes onto the food.

536
00:34:14,615 --> 00:34:19,745
"The one who made this is me."

537
00:34:21,330 --> 00:34:25,042
However,
not all the lies have been uncovered yet.

538
00:34:25,126 --> 00:34:26,836
What?

539
00:34:27,753 --> 00:34:31,716
The real reason Gaudí
entrusted the work to Berenguer.

540
00:34:34,302 --> 00:34:37,847
I'm telling you, it's true!
It's my restaurant!

541
00:34:37,930 --> 00:34:41,392
I'll poach you from Trompe-l'œil too,
so come with me!

542
00:34:44,312 --> 00:34:45,521
Huh?

543
00:34:47,773 --> 00:34:48,900
Why?

544
00:34:56,115 --> 00:34:58,075
He said this place closed down!

545
00:34:59,827 --> 00:35:01,204
What is the matter?

546
00:35:01,287 --> 00:35:02,622
Huh?

547
00:35:04,582 --> 00:35:07,710
I believe today will be the final check.

548
00:35:08,252 --> 00:35:10,421
Are you confident in what you created?

549
00:35:10,504 --> 00:35:11,464
Yes.

550
00:35:12,131 --> 00:35:15,676
I've completed your ideal design,
Chef Kajiwara.

551
00:35:33,444 --> 00:35:34,737
What are you implying?

552
00:35:35,780 --> 00:35:37,156
It's just as you see.

553
00:35:38,324 --> 00:35:42,161
You have no intention
of opening a new restaurant.

554
00:35:42,912 --> 00:35:46,832
No, rather,
you would hate it if a new one was built.

555
00:35:49,377 --> 00:35:53,089
About a year ago, you started
entrusting menu development,

556
00:35:53,631 --> 00:35:59,095
course setup, and everything else
about the restaurant to Mr. Higuchi.

557
00:35:59,804 --> 00:36:01,847
Why did you do that?

558
00:36:03,432 --> 00:36:04,558
Over 20 years,

559
00:36:04,642 --> 00:36:08,229
I have taught Higuchi
everything to know about cooking.

560
00:36:09,730 --> 00:36:14,402
He possesses the skill to handle
Trompe-l'œil. That is all.

561
00:36:15,820 --> 00:36:20,032
Is that also the reason you don't taste
the dishes Mr. Higuchi makes?

562
00:36:20,116 --> 00:36:21,117
Yes.

563
00:36:31,002 --> 00:36:34,588
This is the medicine
you've been taking for the past year.

564
00:36:36,132 --> 00:36:38,592
This is zinc, isn't it?

565
00:36:45,933 --> 00:36:50,271
Could you show me
the design you made last time, again?

566
00:36:51,147 --> 00:36:52,356
Yes.

567
00:37:04,702 --> 00:37:07,496
By having my cooking praised,

568
00:37:07,580 --> 00:37:11,667
I earned stars,
was fawned over by the media,

569
00:37:12,752 --> 00:37:16,464
gained fame,
and I lost sight of what was important.

570
00:37:18,341 --> 00:37:19,383
But this…

571
00:37:20,593 --> 00:37:21,761
This is…

572
00:37:22,762 --> 00:37:24,055
This design…

573
00:37:24,555 --> 00:37:26,474
It called out to me.

574
00:37:27,600 --> 00:37:33,856
"Do I want to cling to fame so badly,
I'm willing to tell lies?"

575
00:37:34,440 --> 00:37:36,442
What happened a year ago?

576
00:37:38,819 --> 00:37:40,863
I lost my sense of taste.

577
00:37:41,947 --> 00:37:46,327
An aftereffect from the virus
during the pandemic two years ago.

578
00:37:46,410 --> 00:37:48,954
I have a taste disorder.

579
00:37:51,207 --> 00:37:52,583
Would you like to taste it?

580
00:37:53,542 --> 00:37:54,877
No, it's fine.

581
00:37:55,628 --> 00:37:57,671
That's why you take zinc,

582
00:37:58,464 --> 00:38:01,342
because it is said to be effective
for taste disorders.

583
00:38:11,143 --> 00:38:16,315
When I lost my sense of taste,
I thought about closing the restaurant.

584
00:38:17,191 --> 00:38:20,277
However, I couldn't do that
because of the sponsors.

585
00:38:23,781 --> 00:38:26,117
So, I entrusted it to Higuchi.

586
00:38:27,952 --> 00:38:32,331
I acknowledge Higuchi's skill.
That part wasn't a lie.

587
00:38:34,875 --> 00:38:36,419
Right around then,

588
00:38:37,086 --> 00:38:41,090
you were asked by your sponsors
to open a new restaurant.

589
00:38:43,342 --> 00:38:45,594
I was introduced to a contractor,

590
00:38:45,678 --> 00:38:47,972
and everything was arranged
without my input.

591
00:38:50,683 --> 00:38:55,813
Even though, in this condition,
I can't open a new restaurant.

592
00:38:56,814 --> 00:38:59,275
You thought of entrusting
the new location to him?

593
00:39:00,943 --> 00:39:02,903
I did think about it.

594
00:39:03,571 --> 00:39:05,614
Higuchi seemed up for it as well.

595
00:39:06,615 --> 00:39:07,825
However,

596
00:39:09,034 --> 00:39:12,663
if I did that,
what would happen to this restaurant?

597
00:39:14,582 --> 00:39:18,335
This restaurant, which Higuchi
currently handles entirely.

598
00:39:20,713 --> 00:39:22,214
It would crumble.

599
00:39:23,841 --> 00:39:25,134
Exactly.

600
00:39:25,843 --> 00:39:31,140
That's why you wouldn't accept any design,
right, Mr. Kajiwara?

601
00:39:31,640 --> 00:39:32,725
Yeah.

602
00:39:40,399 --> 00:39:41,525
But…

603
00:39:43,486 --> 00:39:45,488
I've decided to accept it now.

604
00:39:48,199 --> 00:39:49,283
I will accept…

605
00:39:50,326 --> 00:39:51,952
this design.

606
00:39:57,458 --> 00:40:00,169
I bet you knew about the relationship

607
00:40:00,252 --> 00:40:03,714
between Chef Kajiwara
and Mr. Higuchi from the start.

608
00:40:03,797 --> 00:40:07,885
You used this strategy just to make
Mr. Higuchi open his eyes.

609
00:40:10,930 --> 00:40:14,225
There is more to the story
of Gaudí and Berenguer.

610
00:40:14,767 --> 00:40:15,726
What?

611
00:40:16,810 --> 00:40:20,564
Berenguer unfortunately
passed away at a young age.

612
00:40:21,607 --> 00:40:23,859
At that time, Gaudí said,

613
00:40:25,110 --> 00:40:31,242
"I have lost my right hand."

614
00:40:33,786 --> 00:40:38,499
I hope Gaudí's feelings
will reach Berenguer's heart.

615
00:40:40,543 --> 00:40:42,294
THE RADIANT GASTRONOMY GUIDE

616
00:40:56,850 --> 00:40:57,977
Chef.

617
00:41:03,566 --> 00:41:04,775
This restaurant…

618
00:41:06,026 --> 00:41:09,280
I can no longer manage it.

619
00:41:09,905 --> 00:41:11,323
-So--
-Higuchi.

620
00:41:15,286 --> 00:41:18,497
I'm sorry for everything.

621
00:41:20,457 --> 00:41:21,542
What?

622
00:41:31,176 --> 00:41:32,761
It must have been painful.

623
00:41:34,054 --> 00:41:36,473
Having your cooking praised,

624
00:41:37,558 --> 00:41:39,893
yet not being recognized yourself.

625
00:41:39,977 --> 00:41:41,020
But…

626
00:41:41,604 --> 00:41:42,896
It's all right now.

627
00:41:45,941 --> 00:41:47,443
This is your restaurant.

628
00:41:48,777 --> 00:41:49,862
Chef…

629
00:41:56,702 --> 00:41:59,955
I leave Trompe-l'œil in your hands.

630
00:42:01,832 --> 00:42:02,916
Chef Higuchi.

631
00:42:16,013 --> 00:42:17,264
I'm sorry.

632
00:42:17,348 --> 00:42:19,808
I failed to design the new restaurant.

633
00:42:19,892 --> 00:42:23,646
What are you talking about?
Thanks to you, everyone was saved.

634
00:42:23,729 --> 00:42:26,565
Me, Chef Kajiwara, and Mr. Higuchi too.

635
00:42:27,358 --> 00:42:28,400
Thank you.

636
00:42:29,318 --> 00:42:30,569
It's nothing.

637
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:33,364
More importantly, Sabayama.

638
00:42:33,447 --> 00:42:35,282
I got the manager's approval!

639
00:42:35,366 --> 00:42:37,242
-What?
-I told you, right?

640
00:42:37,326 --> 00:42:40,829
That we should work together again
at Kyosue Construction.

641
00:42:41,872 --> 00:42:45,167
But I couldn't put the design together.

642
00:42:45,250 --> 00:42:47,544
That doesn't matter anymore!

643
00:42:50,089 --> 00:42:51,215
Come back to us.

644
00:43:04,603 --> 00:43:07,523
Thank you for inviting me. I'm happy.

645
00:43:09,024 --> 00:43:12,194
But, I'm going to try
my best where I am now.

646
00:43:13,362 --> 00:43:17,032
Those guys,
they can't do anything without me.

647
00:43:17,533 --> 00:43:18,659
Really?

648
00:43:19,743 --> 00:43:23,831
Why? You said you wished
you hadn't quit our company, right?

649
00:43:25,290 --> 00:43:26,375
I'm sorry.

650
00:43:26,458 --> 00:43:28,252
-I'm sorry!
-The heck?

651
00:43:29,795 --> 00:43:31,088
I am terribly sorry.

652
00:43:31,171 --> 00:43:36,385
I was hoping to have you
handle the culinary side…

653
00:43:37,886 --> 00:43:40,431
I see.

654
00:43:41,056 --> 00:43:42,850
I don't really mind.

655
00:43:44,184 --> 00:43:46,437
Even if you have no sense of taste.

656
00:43:46,520 --> 00:43:50,983
Honestly, what we need is your name.

657
00:43:52,192 --> 00:43:55,738
The name Chef Kohei Kajiwara.

658
00:43:56,947 --> 00:44:00,701
Then all the more reason
why I cannot do it.

659
00:44:03,704 --> 00:44:04,955
Excuse me.

660
00:44:12,755 --> 00:44:14,798
Is it fine to leave it like this?

661
00:44:15,632 --> 00:44:20,554
We were ready to announce him
as the food manager for the Expo.

662
00:44:21,180 --> 00:44:23,015
Tough luck.

663
00:44:24,183 --> 00:44:25,893
Shall we look for a replacement?

664
00:44:25,976 --> 00:44:27,144
Understood.

665
00:44:27,227 --> 00:44:30,981
Also, I've taken care
of the Hakari Architecture Office.

666
00:44:35,027 --> 00:44:38,614
Everyone, thank you so much for your help!

667
00:44:38,697 --> 00:44:42,034
That was a close one.
That medicine was just a lucky guess.

668
00:44:42,117 --> 00:44:43,452
I was so nervous.

669
00:44:43,535 --> 00:44:45,370
Inside that bottle was ramune candy.

670
00:44:45,996 --> 00:44:48,874
In the end, Mr. Uramawashi saved us again.

671
00:44:48,957 --> 00:44:50,626
Yeah.

672
00:44:51,126 --> 00:44:54,713
Now I owe Mr. Uramawashi a favor too,

673
00:44:56,048 --> 00:44:58,175
so let's continue working together!

674
00:44:58,258 --> 00:45:00,052
-Yeah.
-Do your best, Sabayama.

675
00:45:01,303 --> 00:45:02,596
Shouldn't it be "Mr."?

676
00:45:02,679 --> 00:45:04,848
Mr. Sabayama?

677
00:45:04,932 --> 00:45:07,434
It's not like I'm your junior
or something!

678
00:45:07,518 --> 00:45:08,519
Excuse me.

679
00:45:11,480 --> 00:45:13,315
Is the boss, Mr. Kureta, here?

680
00:45:13,398 --> 00:45:15,484
That would be me.

681
00:45:17,277 --> 00:45:20,781
We are here for an inspection
from the district's Building Division.

682
00:45:22,699 --> 00:45:23,992
I am Tachibana.

683
00:45:24,993 --> 00:45:26,578
We ask for your cooperation.

684
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:43,971
There is something I must tell him.

685
00:45:44,054 --> 00:45:45,806
Officials came for an inspection.

686
00:45:45,889 --> 00:45:47,975
So your business was basically suspended?

687
00:45:48,058 --> 00:45:48,934
You know her, right?

688
00:45:49,017 --> 00:45:50,310
Probe into it a little.

689
00:45:50,394 --> 00:45:51,603
Don't mess with me!

690
00:45:51,687 --> 00:45:53,730
Are you Representative Furuse's henchman?

691
00:45:53,814 --> 00:45:56,066
Shall I help you out, as usual?

692
00:45:56,149 --> 00:45:57,067
Congratulations.

693
00:45:59,611 --> 00:46:01,780
I'll leave the rest to you.

694
00:46:02,281 --> 00:46:03,240
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

